# ONE RULE. Resist adding a second one for the demo — that is what broke
# it, twice, and the second time worse than the first.
#
# WHAT WAS MEASURED ON THE LIVE DEPLOYMENT, because none of this is
# guessable from Cloudflare's documentation:
#
#   `/*  /index.html  200` behaves as a REWRITE, and only on an asset
#   miss. A real file always wins over it — which is why /demo/ served
#   the demo's own index.html the whole time this file also carried a
#   /demo/* rule.
#
#   Any OTHER 200 rule does not rewrite. `/demo/*  /demo-shell.html 200`
#   was served as a 308 REDIRECT to /demo-shell, and it fired ahead of
#   the static files. So every demo URL — including /demo/ itself — was
#   bounced to /demo-shell, where the app booted with basename="/demo"
#   on a path that is not under /demo, matched no route, and rendered a
#   blank page.
#
#   And `/demo/*  /demo/index.html  200`, the rule that lived here
#   before that, was silently DROPPED — a destination matching its own
#   source pattern — which is why demo deep links fell through to the
#   root app and showed the landing page.
#
# Three behaviours, three different failures, none of them documented.
# The demo therefore does not use a rule at all: the build writes a real
# .html file for every route the router declares (demoRouteShells in
# vite.config.js), and a real file is the one thing that has worked at
# every step of this.
